      "writtenOn": "2014-05-05T20:12:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do this like the other commands we\u0027ve added recently, where there\u0027s a subcommand field in the params to ask for different things.  That\u0027s easier to understand than passing offset\u003d(some strange number) to return special info.\n\nenum ec_port80_subcmd {\n   EC_PORT80_GET_INFO \u003d 0,\n   EC_PORT80_READ_BUFFER,\n};\n\nstruct ec_params_port80_read {\n  uint8 subcmd;\n\n  union {\n    struct {\n      uint32_t offset;\n      uint32_t num_entries;\n    } read_buffer;\n  }\n};\n\nstruct ec_response_port80_read {\n  union {\n\n    struct {\n      uint32_t writes;\n      uint32_t last_boot;\n    } get_info;\n\n    struct {\n      uint16_t codes[64];\n    }\n  }\n};",
